data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS","toolCallId":"call_a1c9b4244fc64abb89412320","delta":"{\"file_path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/SKILL.md\",\"limit\":400,\"offset\":0}"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_END","toolCallId":"call_a1c9b4244fc64abb89412320"}

data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_a1c9b4244fc64abb89412320","messageId":"8f667c0c-be81-437f-8e9f-9b123acede9f","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/ui-plugin-development/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"1: ---\\n2: name: ui-plugin-development\\n3: description: Inspect or customize UI Plugins; propose missing project capabilities through a bounded user-confirmed development plan, reusing existing approved scopes.\\n4: compatibility: Agent UI Plugin Creator Phase 8 permits writes under project plugins and AppUIModel composition.\\n5: allowed-tools: enable_creator_tools takeover_plugin_source ask_user_question read_file ls glob grep edit_file prepare_ui_plugin_development create_ui_plugin mutate_ui_plugin_source prepare_ui_service_contract_change create_ui_service_contract mutate_ui_service_contract inspect_ui_capabilities inspect_ui_plugin_delivery inspect_ui_project inspect_app_ui_model inspect_ui_slots list_ui_plugins inspect_ui_plugin preflight_ui_plugin_placement inspect_ui_services inspect_ui_plugin_source_references inspect_agent_ui_sources apply_agent_ui_source_item mutate_app_ui_model validate_creator_changes\\n6: ---\\n7: \\n8: # UI Plugin development\\n9: \\n10: This Skill applies to frontend Plugin source/application authoring. The system\\n11: prompt owns general evidence, authorization and completion rules; this Skill\\n12: adds Plugin-specific contracts, not an additional investigation checklist.\\n13: Use the smallest relevant section/reference. A resolved existing target does not\\n14: require a full capability inventory, a new UI-system decision or a nearest\\n15: consumer example before it can be modified.\\n16: \\n17: ## Ownership and admission\\n18: \\n19: Project-owned application props, children, renderers and scoped styles are ordinary\\n20: editable code. Inspect the exact target and any concrete unknown contract; edit\\n21: within the user's request. Public npm component use does not require implementation\\n22: source, extraction or takeover. Existing source-owned Plugin edits keep the current\\n23: ownership, upstream provenance and BASE; do not repeat successful takeover consent.\\n24: Only actual npm implementation edits require `takeover_plugin_source` and its\\n25: explicit user agreement. Canonical Runtime/Context, vendor and generated registries\\n26: remain protected. A thin wrapper's omitted public seam is not justification for\\n27: requiring takeover.\\n28: \\n29: Before first new Plugin source or new business behavior, the Host must authorize\\n30: the bounded `prepare_ui_plugin_development` plan through its actual start/adjust/defer\\n31: question. The current request identifies the desired work, not approval of an\\n32: unseen implementation plan; a matching approved plan is reused without asking again. A normal existing\\n33: Plugin customization does not need a new development approval. Once the relevant API/source lacks the behavior, propose a bounded implementation;\\n34: do not search for the same missing operation in unrelated components. Required Service\\n35: contracts may be included as relatedServices in that one decision. For a genuinely new\\n36: Plugin, consult [authoring contracts](references/authoring-contracts.md) for admission,\\n37: manifest/placement, Service/data and delivery obligations. For a new visual Plugin\\n38: or actual UI-system choice also consult [UI selection](references/default-ui-composition.md).\\n39: Do not load new-Plugin investigation requirements for a local presentation repair.\\n40: \\n41: ## Local change evidence\\n42: \\n43: Read the existing files that will change, using the actual supplied sourceRoot and\\n44: owner paths. `manifest.json` declares identity/data/capabilities; `definition.ts`\\n45: joins manifest and component; `index.tsx` owns composition/behavior; imported\\n46: stylesheets own presentation. Read a neighboring consumer only for wiring that\\n47: is actually unknown. An npm implementation need not appear in local search.\\n48: \\n49: `inspect_ui_plugin` returns application ownership, public APIs and parent semantic\\n50: composition where declared. sharedModule selects the installed public module;\\n51: use the root module for presentation controls and /contracts for Plugin types.\\n52: Use returned parameterContracts; follow exact parameterQueries only when a required\\n53: signature is missing. `$element` accesses an array/index element, not React props.\\n54: An unavailable guessed symbol is not a missing capability. Preserve declared\\n55: composition slots when appending controls; replacement props can replace them.\\n56: \\n57: Public types establish invocation shape, not rendered styling. Package-owned\\n58: presentationContract describes raw versus styled components, asset requirements\\n59: and Portal ownership. For a visual defect follow the current owned entry's CSS\\n60: imports and inspect the relevant cascade. Re-querying types cannot establish\\n61: centering. Public overlay composites may own their own Portal and Backdrop;\\n62: respect that composition and retain the existing AgentUIRoot theme container.\\n63: Use the public Trigger/Close/focus APIs. Local dialog state or scoped popup\\n64: positioning does not introduce a Service, Agent action, Runtime replacement or\\n65: source takeover. Verify requested placement, closing and focus in the actual Host.\\n66: \\n67: ## Editing constraints\\n68: \\n69: Freshly read existing edit targets in the current run; old messages/handoff are\\n70: navigation, not current read evidence. `edit_file_from_read` edits a stable range;\\n71: `edit_file` handles small local changes; `mutate_ui_plugin_source` makes one atomic\\n72: Plugin-local transaction with edit/create entries. Re-read and reconcile affected\\n73: files after stale-content errors. Do not hand-edit `registry.generated.ts`, the\\n74: AppUIModel JSON or composition-revision metadata; use their Host tools.\\n75: \\n76: Preserve the target's UI library, enabled capabilities, scope bridge, semantic\\n77: slots and original approval/interrupt/error renderers. New user/screen-reader copy\\n78: uses the unified domain locale namespace with en-US/zh-CN parity; never patch\\n79: vendor for localization. Read locale targets when changing them, not for every\\n80: style edit. Do not invent new per-Plugin i18n or Service abstractions.\\n81: \\n82: Styles must be imported and scoped to owned classes/data attributes; no global\\n83: resets, Host ancestor selectors, Runtime/Portal changes or vendor overrides.\\n84: Own box-sizing, min-width and responsive maximum size. Flex/grid children must\\n85: shrink and long text wrap; overlays need bounded dimensions appropriate to the\\n86: actual container. Static heuristics are not visual acceptance. The specialized\\n87: responsive-repair proposal tool is not currently exposed by any Creator tool\\n88: group. For ordinary authorized responsive CSS changes, freshly read the owned\\n89: stylesheet, use the available file-edit tools and validate the current revision.\\n90: If the user explicitly requests the unavailable specialized proposal tool,\\n91: explain that limitation; do not claim to have invoked it.\\n92: \\n93: ## Validation and outcome\\n94: \\n95: Validate source changes at the current revision; include the build for new visual\\n96: Plugins or dependency/style integration as required. Composition changes use fresh\\n97: AppUIModel evidence and normal Host mutation/verification tools. Creation/catalog\\n98: synchronization is not mounting: newly created capabilities must be composed when\\n99: requested, and the final revision validated. Consume checks already performed by\\n100: the Host rather than duplicating them. Respect returned repair limits.\\n101: \\n102: Keep static, Runtime and browser evidence distinct. Current tests/types or empty\\n103: Runtime errors do not prove popup geometry, keyboard behavior or focus. Validate\\n104: the requested interactions using available authorized browser/test evidence; report\\n105: missing infrastructure or stale evidence precisely. Do not label incomplete work\\n106: as already satisfied or reopen unrelated discovery when verification is unavailable.\\n107: \",\"hash\":\"2095749f75d9cb178b5188b624c16e39bd391bffbf9448e0a8e8a9d3f5c46ec6\",\"totalLines\":107,\"nextOffset\":null}}","role":"tool"}

